{
  "configuration_id": "config_030",
  "reason": "The strongest evidence is RNA-only scvi_n200 with multiprofile (config_005/006, ~0.65), while image-only ResNet50 is weak (config_011, 0.33). The key uncertainty is whether adding image features to the strong RNA model improves validation accuracy or adds noise. config_030 keeps the already-tested strong RNA setting (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) and the already-tested image setting (ResNet50, multiprofile, avgpool), introducing only concat fusion. This allows direct comparison with config_005 and config_011, isolating the effect of multimodal fusion before varying fusion type, aggregation, or image encoder, making it the most informative next step under a limited budget."
}

